        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a5f86d5e-eeba-5b8b-bd19-f252de3e824a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Agee, Nelly Sachs, Davis Grubb, Matthew Mead, Ruth Mead, Johannes Bobrowski\n- Works: A Death in the Family, The Night of the Hunter, The Night of the Hunter novel\n- Awards: Pulitzer Prize, Nobel Prize in Literature\n- Roles: film critics, poets, translators\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1940s, James Agee was one of the most influential film critics in the United States.\n- In 1953, Davis Grubb published the novel The Night of the Hunter.\n- In 1957, James Agee's autobiographical novel A Death in the Family was published.\n- In 1957, James Agee wrote the screenplay for the film The Night of the Hunter, and it was based on Davis Grubb's 1953 novel of the same name.\n- In 1958, James Agee posthumously received the Pulitzer Prize for A Death in the Family.\n- In 1966, Nelly Sachs was awarded the Nobel Prize in Literature.\n- Matthew Mead, born in 1924 in Buckinghamshire and died in 2009, was an English poet and, with his wife Ruth, a translator of German poets including Johannes Bobrowski and Nelly Sachs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7cb9e075-a21b-5669-ad61-c2f653e210af",
        "text": "Page: James Agee. Sentence: In the 1940s, he was one of the most influential film critics in the U.S. His autobiographical novel, \"A Death in the Family\" (1957), won the author a posthumous 1958 Pulitzer Prize.\nPage: Nelly Sachs. Sentence: She was awarded with the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1966.\nPage: The Night of the Hunter (film). Sentence: The screenplay by James Agee was based on the 1953 novel of the same name by Davis Grubb.\nPage: Matthew Mead (poet). Sentence: Matthew Mead (born 1924, Buckinghamshire, died 2009) was an English poet as well as a translator, with his wife Ruth, of German poets, including Johannes Bobrowski and Nelly Sachs.",
